ink is  really  quite good that sums up the  cynic attitude has to do with the kind  of life  that we we live right when someone  declared that  life is an evil that life is bad  he corrected him he said it's not life  itself that's bad  it's living poorly or  living ill living badly  um cacos in this as an adjective  in the greek and so you know that's a  really great way to think about it it's  life is what we make of it the cynics  decide that they're going to make of it  a way to truly be happy they call this  the royal  road to happiness it's a very difficult  path to pursue but diogenes thought that  he was helping out  his fellow members of athens he's not  actually an athenian  himself but doing something similar to  what socrates is doing  trying to call people's attention back  to what's really  important and to tell them that their  priorities are off and to do so  precisely by the way that he's living  you could say  if diogenes can do it maybe i can do it  too  and so we have the possibility of not  living badly but instead  living a happy life following the  cynic way of living that diogenes  perhaps  took to one of its extremes  you

